#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Offline stand-in for the codexbar CLI, for UI smoke runs and the devkit.

Point the extension at it with CODEXBAR_BIN=<this file>. It never reads
accounts, credentials or the network. STUB_CODEXBAR_SYNC=0 makes it behave
like upstream's CLI: no `codexbar sync` and no /sync/* routes in `serve`.
STUB_CODEXBAR_REPORT=1 adds a capability report to /health.
STUB_CODEXBAR_PAIRED=1 (with sync) pretends this Machine is in a Sync Group
with one other Machine, so the Machines tab and the paired Settings page show.
STUB_CODEXBAR_ISSUES=1 makes /usage return one healthy provider and one of
each provider error state, for the issues banner and Details dialog.
STUB_CODEXBAR_ACCOUNTS=1 advertises providerAccountRows on /health and answers
/usage?accounts=all with two OpenRouter Provider Accounts (Work active, the
Personal key failing) next to a single-account Claude row; plain /usage gets
the single-account rows an older CLI would send. STUB_CODEXBAR_ACCOUNTS=3 adds
a third OpenRouter account, Spare, at 12% (the most headroom). Both also
advertise the account actions: /accounts/kinds offers `key` for OpenRouter, and
/accounts/add, /accounts/rename and /accounts/remove change the OpenRouter
accounts in memory (keys are checked for presence and never stored). Like
serve, those need the X-UsageBar-Action-Token header to match
USAGEBAR_SERVE_ACTION_TOKEN (403 otherwise, and for any Origin header); without
the variable they are refused and /health leaves the account actions out.
STUB_CODEXBAR_CLAUDE_SWAP=1 (with ACCOUNTS) makes Claude's rows claude-swap's:
two slots on /usage?accounts=all (work active, personal stale with its
error), and the active slot's row on plain /usage.
STUB_CODEXBAR_CLAUDE_SWITCH=1 (with CLAUDE_SWAP) adds a third slot, spare,
marks the inactive slots claude-swap can activate with canSwitch, advertises
providerAccountSwitch, and answers POST /accounts/switch in memory after a
short delay (STUB_CODEXBAR_SWITCH_DELAY seconds, default 1.5); the next
/usage after a switch takes as long, so both progress phases show. Switching
back to work fails like a switch result naming the wrong slot.
STUB_CODEXBAR_CODEX_ACCOUNTS=1 advertises providerAccountRows and answers
/usage?accounts=all with three Codex Provider Accounts: the everyday login
(active) and two managed accounts, one of them failing; plain /usage gets the
same three rows untagged, as serve sends them.
STUB_CODEXBAR_CLAUDE_SWAP_ADD=1 (with ACCOUNTS) offers Add account… on Claude
(kind `claude-swap`, providerAccountAddClaudeSwap on /health). POST
/accounts/claude-swap/detect (action token required) answers "not installed"
the first time and installed after that, as if the install offer worked.
`codexbar claude add-account` prints the three steps and "done"; it runs
nothing, but with an XDG_DATA_HOME of its own it leaves a flag file there
($XDG_DATA_HOME/usagebar-stub-claude-added) that makes serve list a third
claude-swap slot, as if the add had worked.
With an action token, CODEX_ACCOUNTS also offers `cli-login` for Codex on
/accounts/kinds, and `stub-codexbar codex-accounts add` acts out the add helper:
it runs the fake `codex` named by STUB_CODEX_BIN (never a codex from PATH) as
`<STUB_CODEX_BIN> login` with CODEX_HOME set to a new home under
$XDG_DATA_HOME/CodexBar/managed-codex-homes, then records the email the fake
wrote to that home's auth.json in $XDG_DATA_HOME/CodexBar/managed-codex-accounts.json,
which serve then lists as one more managed row. It refuses to run without an
XDG_DATA_HOME of its own, so it never writes the real data directory.
STUB_CODEXBAR_SHOWCASE=1 is for looking around in a devkit rather than for a
smoke: it turns on PAIRED, ACCOUNTS=3, CLAUDE_SWAP, CLAUDE_SWITCH and
CODEX_ACCOUNTS together, and /usage answers with all of their rows plus the
ISSUES providers that none of those cover (failing Gemini, Copilot and Cursor,
healthy OpenCode Go), so every case shows in one popover.
STUB_CODEXBAR_HEALTH_FAIL_SECS=N answers /health with 503 for the first N
seconds after serve starts, like a serve that isn't ready yet.
"""

